import json,platform,subprocess,datetime
from pathlib import Path
s=json.load(open('results/benchmark_summary.json'))
s['environment']={'date':datetime.datetime.now(datetime.timezone.utc).isoformat(),'platform':platform.platform(),'compiler':subprocess.check_output(['g++','--version'],text=True).splitlines()[0],'cpu':next((x.split(':',1)[1].strip() for x in Path('/proc/cpuinfo').read_text().splitlines() if x.startswith('model name')),'unknown'),'flags':'-std=c++17 -O2 -pthread','logicalCpuCount':__import__('os').cpu_count()}
Path('results/benchmark_summary.json').write_text(json.dumps(s,indent=2)+'\n')
Path('results/BENCHMARK.md').write_text(f'''# Measured results\n\nRun: {s['environment']['date']}\n\nCompiler: {s['environment']['compiler']}\n\nCPU: {s['environment']['cpu']}\n\nFlags: `{s['environment']['flags']}`\n\nNine timed rounds, 200,000 operations per round, after warmup. Alternating baseline/instrumented order. One producer; 16 integer recurrence steps per operation with a volatile checksum sink.\n\n| Metric | Result |\n|---|---:|\n| Median baseline | {s['baselineMedianNs']:.3f} ns/op |\n| Median instrumented | {s['instrumentedMedianNs']:.3f} ns/op |\n| Difference of medians | {s['incrementalMedianNs']:.3f} ns/op |\n| Event size | {s['eventSizeBytes']} bytes |\n| Ring capacity | {s['capacity']} events |\n| Event array storage | {s['eventStorageBytes']} bytes |\n\nThese are synthetic measurements on a shared Linux host, not console benchmarks or production overhead. The measured increment includes two steady-clock calls, two bounded name copies, mutex locking, and ring storage. Event-array size excludes the recorder object, allocator metadata, mutex, and temporary export snapshots. No allocations occur in `record()` after construction; snapshot/export allocate. With four producers the mutex serializes recording. The 4-thread demo validates correctness, not throughput scaling. Nested span totals double-count enclosing work and must not be interpreted as aggregate wall time.\n''')
print(json.dumps(s,indent=2))
